THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

This licence covers the laboratory infrastructure authored in this repository:
the orchestrator, the acquisition and provenance code, the scenario runners,
the build recipes and the documentation.

It does NOT cover the vendored upstream archives under `scenarios/*/files/`,
which remain under their own licences and are redistributed unmodified:

  Father        https://github.com/mav8557/Father        Unlicense
  Diamorphine   https://github.com/m0nad/Diamorphine     BSD-3-Clause
  bad-bpf       https://github.com/pathtofile/bad-bpf    BSD-3-Clause / GPL-2.0

Each scenario's `*.lock.yml` records the pinned upstream commit, the archive
hash and the licence. Any patch applied to an upstream source is hash-pinned
separately and documented in the same file.

INTENDED USE

This repository is research infrastructure for a master's thesis on post-mortem
Linux digital forensics. Its scenarios execute only in isolated, disposable,
authorised virtual machines, and exist to produce reproducible evidence for
defensive forensic analysis. It is not a penetration-testing toolkit and
provides no capability for use against systems you do not own or are not
authorised to test.
